  "id": "set-theory-model-theory",
  "title": "Set Theory and Model Theory: From Collections to Models",
  "categories": [
    "Mathematics"
  ],
  "summary": "An audio-first mathematical foundations course explaining axiomatic set construction, cardinality, ordinals, choice, the syntax and semantics of first-order theories, compactness, elementary substructures, and the distinction between completeness and incompleteness. Worked arguments bridge elementary proof habits to formalization.",
  "assumed_background": [
    "Basic sets, functions, proof by contradiction, and mathematical induction. First-order syntax is introduced from scratch. Linear algebra examples assume familiarity with independence and span."
  ],
